<title>USA: Lowell Hospital, Mass., repriced, yields lowered.</title>
<headline>Lowell Hospital, Mass., repriced, yields lowered.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>PaineWebber Inc said Tuesday it repriced Massachusetts Health and Educational Facilities Authority's $34.9 million bond deal, for Lowell General Hospital, lowering yields five basis points in the 1997 through 1999 maturities.</p>
<p>The repricing follows:  </p>
<p>MASSACHUSETTS HEALTH AND EDUCATIONAL FACILITIES</p>
<p>AUTHORITY REVENUE BONDS, LOWELL GENERAL HOSPITAL ISSUE</p>
<p>RE: $34,865,000* SERIES B</p>
<p>THIS ISSUE WILL BE IN BOOK ENTRY FORM THROUGH THE FACILITIES</p>
<p>OF DTC</p>
<p>VERBAL AWARD.</p>
<p>  MOODY'S: Aaa (FSA INS)   S&amp;P: AAA (FSA)	 FITCH: NAF</p>
<p>	     UNDERLYING: A3	 UNDERLYING: A-  UNDERLYING: A-</p>
